Welcome.

The best way to deal with nymphs is to meet as few as possible, 
so try and curb your reckless fountain quaffing (tough to do, I 
still sip 'em). Fountains aside, nymphs are a lazy sort and you 
might notice many start asleep.  If you don't wake them they 
won't bug you.  Becareful of ^squeaky boards, kicking down doors, 
blowing tin whistles, trapped doors, gas spores and other 
exploding creatures (e and y) all of which make noise and disturb 
the nymph's harmless slumber. Second, the best way to deal with 
nearly ANY early monster... let your cat(pet) do it. Get a feel 
for "dancing**"  around your cat, keeping out of the nymph's 
reach while keeping her in the claws of your kitten.

**let me try an illustration

  +-----+
  |     |
  |  n  |    < --- offending nymph.
  | @f  |    < --- hero and loyal feline.
  |      ##
  +-----+

The best move here is SE, down-right. The nymph will follow, 
moving to your previous position. You'll keep moving on diagonals 
and she'll keep getting bit by the kitten, without a chance to 
rob you.


Anyway, another effective tactic is to carry lots of light junk, 
a few rocks, all gems, daggers, knives, darts, arrows, bolts, 
dwarf cloaks, etc... light items that'll increase the nymph's 
chance of stealing something useless (just never stay burdened) . 
Once she starts taking your gear? Well, hope she doesn't get 
ahold of your CoMR, but remember that only Force Bolt will break 
her mirrior, other offensive spells and wands won't.  Magic 
Missiles, Lightning. Also fire and cold... just don't always 
count on getting her Potion of Obj Detect -or that potion of gain 
ability she stole- back in one piece

Otherwise, the tactics you mentioned were fine.  When throwing 
things, remember to start early and retreat if you can. If you 
really don't have anything with which to take her out, just leave 
the level for a bit and come back when more prepared. Nymphs 
themselves will never level teleport, but they can escape up and 
down stairs, and they are vulnerable to trap doors, holes, and 
level teleport traps (If a nymph wears your CoMR, will she resist 
a Tele Trap?)

Above all, I preach avoidance. They'll become increasingly less 
of a threat as you advance your character (and find a spellbook 
of magic missile!)

